src/webhookd/signatures.py:123-131 `_build_payload` splices the raw `body` bytes into the template as bytes (line 128: `out += body if key == "body"`), never re-encoding; app.py:167 passes the bytes straight from `_read_body`. Live proof: I signed and posted `{
  "z" : 1,
  "a":  2,
  "u": "caf\u00e9"
}` — whitespace-heavy, non-canonical key order, escaped unicode — and got `202 {"status": "accepted"}`. Any re-serialisation would have changed the bytes and produced a 401.
